======================================================================
Part 1: refinement/convergence study exposing the fixed-grid issue
======================================================================
eps=0.5, target M(y=30.0), refining dy:
  n=    60  dy=0.50000  dy/eps=1.0000   M(30)=0.49655060
  n=   300  dy=0.10000  dy/eps=0.2000   M(30)=0.73969910
  n=  1500  dy=0.02000  dy/eps=0.0400   M(30)=0.83430373
  n=  7500  dy=0.00400  dy/eps=0.0080   M(30)=0.85629351
  n= 30000  dy=0.00100  dy/eps=0.0020   M(30)=0.86054465
  successive differences: ['0.24315', '0.09460', '0.02199', '0.00425']
  Differences shrink monotonically -- genuine convergence, confirms
  s05 (dy=0.25) and s06 (dy=1.0, 2.0) were significantly
  under-resolved at eps=0.5. Finest grid here (dy/eps=0.002) gives
  M(30) = 0.860545 as the trustworthy reference value.

======================================================================
Part 2: ODE reformulation -- symbolic decomposition + cross-check
======================================================================
K_bound(h,z) = A(z)+B(z)*e^{-h/eps}, A:=R(z)+eps*sigma(z), B:=eps-A
residual 0. PASS

ODE reformulation: M(30) = 0.86197090
Finest trapezoid (dy=0.001): M(30) = 0.86054465
relative difference: 1.66e-03
PASS -- ODE reformulation agrees with the properly-converged fine
trapezoid grid to <3e-3 (consistent with Richardson-extrapolating
the trapezoid's own residual discretization error), independently
validating this script's own method (used for everything below).

