Interpretation (reported honestly in ATTEMPT.md Sec 4, not as a
closure claim): M(y) continues to grow (does not plateau) out to
y=200000 for every eps in {0.3,0.5,0.7} tested -- this front's own
sharp kernel bound does NOT establish a finite uniform majorant via
this comparison route, for any eps tested. The growth is far slower
than the naive exponential-Gronwall picture (a genuine, precisely
quantified improvement), and its fitted exponent is the right order
of magnitude as (but does not tightly match) this front's own
admittedly-informal 'slowly-varying M' heuristic prediction.
